    {
      "id": "coriolanus/sceneV_6.1/p@191321",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "BRUTUS.\nOnly make trial what your love can do\nFor Rome, towards Martius.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneV_6.1/p@191321/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 7,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneV_6.1/p@191321/line-2",
          "start": 8,
          "end": 45,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneV_6.1/p@191321/line-3",
          "start": 46,
          "end": 72,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1011033,
        "end": 1011140,
        "line": 38533,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap06/p@191321",
        "anchor": "sceneV_6.1"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "BRUTUS.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "coriolanus/sceneV_6.1/p@191432",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "MENENIUS.\nWell, and say that Martius\nReturn me, as Cominius is returned, unheard,\nWhat then? But as a discontented friend,\nGrief-shot with his unkindness? Say’t be so?",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneV_6.1/p@191432/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneV_6.1/p@191432/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 36,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneV_6.1/p@191432/line-3",
          "start": 37,
          "end": 81,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneV_6.1/p@191432/line-4",
          "start": 82,
          "end": 122,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneV_6.1/p@191432/line-5",
          "start": 123,
          "end": 167,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1011144,
        "end": 1011356,
        "line": 38539,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap06/p@191432",
        "anchor": "sceneV_6.1"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "MENENIUS.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "coriolanus/sceneV_6.1/p@191648",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "SICINIUS.\nYet your good will\nMust have that thanks from Rome after the measure\nAs you intended well.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneV_6.1/p@191648/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneV_6.1/p@191648/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 28,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneV_6.1/p@191648/line-3",
          "start": 29,
          "end": 78,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneV_6.1/p@191648/line-4",
          "start": 79,
          "end": 100,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1011360,
        "end": 1011500,
        "line": 38547,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap06/p@191648",
        "anchor": "sceneV_6.1"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "SICINIUS.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "coriolanus/sceneV_6.1/p@191792",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "MENENIUS.\nI’ll undertake’t.\nI think he’ll hear me. Yet to bite his lip\nAnd hum at good Cominius much unhearts me.\nHe was not taken well; he had not dined.\nThe veins unfilled, our blood is cold, and then\nWe pout upon the morning, are unapt\nTo give or to forgive; but when we have stuffed\nThese pipes and these conveyances of our blood\nWith wine and feeding, we have suppler souls\nThan in our priestlike fasts. Therefore I’ll watch him\nTill he be dieted to my request,\nAnd then I’ll set upon him.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "coriolanus/sceneV_6.1/p@191792/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
